<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Bengali (bn) translations.

    Selected in-app from Account -> Language, which calls AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales.
    That picker existed long before this file did and silently did nothing without it.

    Notes for whoever maintains this:
      - app_name is the brand and stays "Zuhoo".
      - %1$s / %1$d placeholders and their order must match values/strings.xml exactly.
      - Status strings mirror backend enum constants; the constant itself always stays English on
        the wire, only the label here changes.
      - Loanwords (ইমেইল, পাসওয়ার্ড, ইনভয়েস) are used where that is what Bangladeshi users
        actually see in other apps; forcing a Sanskritised equivalent would read as stilted.
-->
